# The Zenodo concept DOI is added under `identifiers:` once the first GitHub
# release mints it. Version and date-released are finalised at release time.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-18"
title: "snp_demux: a Snakemake workflow for SNP-based single-cell demultiplexing"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow that demultiplexes genetically-pooled single-cell RNA-seq
  captures back to their donors from natural genetic variation. It runs
  vireo, demuxlet, freemuxlet and souporcell and combines them into a Demuxafy
  consensus per-cell assignment, with HTML QC reports. The expensive per-cell
  pileups are produced upstream by sc_pileup and consumed here, so the fast
  assignment step can be re-run and re-tuned cheaply. It runs standalone or as a
  git submodule within a DVC-tracked dataset.
type: software
